>>
Rule 1 (dim must be within valid range of input tensor dimensions)
{v_1: int, v_2: tensor} |= 0 - ndim(v_2) ≤ v_1 ∧ v_1 ≤ ndim(v_2) - 1
>>
Rule 2 (input tensor must have floating-point dtype)
{v_2: tensor} |= dtype_(v_2) ≥ 6 ∧ dtype_(v_2) ≤ 8
>>
Rule 3 (input tensor must be at least 1-dimensional)
{v_2: tensor} |= ndim(v_2) ≥ 1
>>
Rule 4 (dim must be negative or non-negative valid index)
{v_1: int, v_2: tensor} |= v_1 ≥ 0 - ndim(v_2) ∧ v_1 < ndim(v_2)
>>
Rule 5 (all dimensions of input tensor must be positive)
{v_2: tensor} |= ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_2) - 1] : shape(v_2, i) > 0
>>
Rule 6 (input tensor dtype must not be char type)
{v_2: tensor} |= dtype_(v_2) ≠ 1
>>
Rule 7 (dim must be less than number of dimensions)
{v_1: int, v_2: tensor} |= v_1 < ndim(v_2)
>>
Rule 8 (dim must be greater than or equal to negative ndim)
{v_1: int, v_2: tensor} |= v_1 ≥ 0 - ndim(v_2)
>>
Rule 9 (input tensor dtype must not be uint8)
{v_2: tensor} |= dtype_(v_2) ≠ 5
>>
Rule 10 (when tensor is 2D dim must be in range)
{v_1: int, v_2: tensor} |= if ndim(v_2) = 2 then v_1 ≥ -2 ∧ v_1 ≤ 1
